   "text": "This structure is brivanib, and its single stereocentre is drawn with a hashed methyl bond.\n\n- **Left ring system:** a 2-methylindole (N\u2013H, methyl on the five-membered ring). The benzene ring carries fluorine next to the ring-fusion carbon, and an aryl ether oxygen on the carbon adjacent to the fluorine-bearing carbon.\n- **Core:** the aryl ether oxygen links to C4 of a pyrrolo[2,1-f][1,2,4]triazine. Its pyrrole ring has a methyl at C5 and an O\u2013CH2\u2013CH(OH)\u2013CH3 ether at C6.\n- **Stereocentre:** the carbon bearing OH has OH drawn up, CH2 to the lower left and CH3 hashed to the lower right, so the hydrogen points toward the viewer. Priorities are OH > CH2O > CH3 > H. Going OH \u2192 CH2 \u2192 CH3 appears counterclockwise from the front, and with H toward the viewer that reverses to clockwise, giving R.\n- **SMILES chirality tag:** in `C[C@@H](O)CO...` the neighbour order is CH3, H, O, CH2. The `@@` tag encodes R for this order, so that is the tag used.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H](O)COc1cn2ncnc(Oc3ccc4[nH]c(C)cc4c3F)c2c1C"
